<title>USA: Wall Street stocks higher at start.</title>
<headline>Wall Street stocks higher at start.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wall Street stocks were higher at the start of trading Monday, following through on Friday's strength despite a weak bond market.</p>
<p>--Dow Industrials up four at 7075.</p>
<p>--Nasdaq Composite up seven at 1313.</p>
<p>--S&amp;P Index up one at 814.</p>
<p>--NYSE advance/decline 391/235</p>
<p>--Nasdaq advance/decline 784/311</p>
<p>--The 30-year long bond off 5/32 to yield 6.89 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1737))</p>
</text>
